From 992c0cb5e3b67a8959eab35fb7609448ad03ce51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:59:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(codex): atomically publish descendant fixture PID
 [daveey]

The fake Codex opens child.pid before writing it. Existence alone therefore
allows the parent to parse an empty string, and teardown repeats that parse,
masking the readiness failure and risking a leaked independent process group.

Write and close a same-directory pending file, install the SIGTERM handler,
then atomically replace child.pid. Keep real close/reaping assertions and add
explicit distinct process-group checks. Freeze and snapshot owned processes
for independent teardown, without reparsing the readiness file.

Deterministically pause the writer after open and before write; the original
publication fails both paused cases. Inject a readiness exception while the
writer is stopped and verify that exception survives and owned processes exit.

Evidence: original source 9a1112a34caa6dd9b51aea20cd3d1acc5dff6c10 has identical
runtime-test bytes to main 2e51977721543a8dc6993d512e7663b380522e76. SIGSTOP after
the original open reproduces ValueError int(''). Regression RED 2 failed/22
passed; GREEN 209 passed across runtime, app-server, session and transport.
scripts/check --base origin/main: all 20 checks pass.
---
 .../test_codex_app_server_runtime.py          | 89 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/agent/transports/test_codex_app_server_runtime.py b/tests/agent/transports/test_codex_app_server_runtime.py
index 963881a65dd211e9d69d6ed631e9d2dbb5af8fc5..63fff589579e6a7cbb564683359fd3290a73fe84 100644
--- a/tests/agent/transports/test_codex_app_server_runtime.py
